/* The stones game's HUD (kar.c: KAR_tick's render calls), the original's sprites in both looks. One pixel of the
   original is 3dp (240 lines over 720 dp); every sprite is placed from the screen's centre, as the original's
   POLY_FT4s are (KAR_renderSprite: setXYWH from the draw offset at 160, 120), with the 4:3 screen centred on a wide
   one. The sprites are the rink's first 4-bit image (VRAM 640, 0: map frzl17, texture4/000), each with its palette
   (the CLUT's x over 16, at y 0x1E6). The later an element, the higher it draws: the original adds them to one slot
   of the ordering table, so the last added is drawn first (name plates, start sign, gauge, scores, hand).

   - KAR_renderNamePlates (KAR_D_8005B4F4): the player's portrait at -140, -95 (32 x 32, texels 0x70, 0x18,
     palette 9) over its blue box at -130, -70 (48 x 32, texels 0x18, 0x38, palette 7); the opponent's at 100, -95
     (texels 0x90, 0x18, palette 10; the second opponent's KAR_D_8005B558: 0xB0, 0x18, palette 12) over its red box
     at 80, -70 (palette 8).
   - KAR_renderScores: two digits of 16 x 16 (palette 1) at y -62, the units at x -105 and 104, the tens 16 left;
     logic.lua picks the glyph (KAR_D_8005B4A0).
   - KAR_renderReadyPrompt (KAR_D_8005B56C): the start sign at -52, 0 (151 x 10, texels 0x68, 0x3E, palette 11).
   - KAR_renderPowerMeter (KAR_D_8005B4CC): the frame at -50 or 50, -50 (48 x 16, texels 0, 0x18, palette 7 the
     player's, 8 the opponent's) and chevron i at the frame's x + 3 i - 3 (16 x 16, texels 0x30, 0x18, palette 7,
     the tenth 3); logic.lua places them.
   - KAR_renderStoneCursor (KAR_D_8005B478): the hand at -120 or 100, row * 30 - 45 (24 x 24, texels 0, 0x28,
     palette 8); logic.lua places it.

   The play or rules question (KAR_tickYesNoPrompt) and the hint pages (KAR_tickHintBox) open the same box at -130,
   42, 262 x 59 from the screen's centre (MAIN_D_80134A10, MAIN_D_80134A28), the story's speech box (#box,
   ../story_textbox/structure.rcss); the hint pages' rows: the speaker's name in text colour 7, then three lines in
   colour 1 (KAR_drawHintPagePenguinmon: setTextColor). The question's selection bar is 94 pixels wide
   (renderSelectionCursor 0x5E). */

body { pointer-events: none; }

#plates img, #ready, #gauge img, #scores img, #hand {
	position: absolute;
	left: 50%;
	top: 50%;
}

#player-face { margin-left: -420dp; margin-top: -285dp; width: 96dp; height: 96dp; }
#player-box { margin-left: -390dp; margin-top: -210dp; width: 144dp; height: 96dp; }
#opponent-face, #opponent-face-2 { margin-left: 300dp; margin-top: -285dp; width: 96dp; height: 96dp; }
#opponent-box { margin-left: 240dp; margin-top: -210dp; width: 144dp; height: 96dp; }

#score-0-tens { margin-left: -363dp; }
#score-0-units { margin-left: -315dp; }
#score-1-tens { margin-left: 264dp; }
#score-1-units { margin-left: 312dp; }
#scores img { margin-top: -186dp; width: 48dp; height: 48dp; }

#ready { margin-left: -156dp; margin-top: 0dp; width: 453dp; height: 30dp; }

#gauge-frame { width: 144dp; height: 48dp; }
#gauge img { margin-top: -150dp; }
.chevron { width: 48dp; height: 48dp; }

#hand { width: 72dp; height: 72dp; }

#question .row.barred .bar { width: 282dp; }

/* The recruit bar (an engine improvement, the option shop_job_bar; the original has none): two lines under the speech
   box, at the bottom of the 4:3 screen (y 222 to 240), as wide as the box: the scores and the throws left, then how
   the match stands and the perfect score while it can still be reached. The modern look's panel; the original look
   gives it the original's box (../skins/original/curling_hud/style.rcss). */
#recruit {
	position: absolute;
	left: 50%;
	top: 664dp;
	width: 786dp;
	height: 54dp;
	margin-left: -390dp;
	padding: 3dp 12dp;
	box-sizing: border-box;
	border-radius: 8dp;
	background-color: #0d121ab8;
	border: 1dp #2e3a4a;
	font-size: 18dp;
	line-height: 23dp;
	color: #c9d3de;
}

.recruit-line {
	display: block;
	position: relative;
	height: 23dp;
}

#recruit-throws, #recruit-perfect {
	position: absolute;
	right: 0;
	top: 0;
}

#recruit-perfect { color: #f0c040; }
#recruit.ahead #recruit-standing { color: #6fdc6f; }
.hidden { display: none; }
